# Line endings, pinned.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows and runs on Linux, in containers and in CI.
# Git's autocrlf converts on checkout, which is fine for source but fatal for
# anything with a shebang: a `#!/usr/bin/env bash` line ending in CRLF makes
# the kernel look for an interpreter called "bash\r", and the error
# ("bad interpreter: No such file or directory") names a file that plainly
# exists. Pinning the executable and container-read files to LF avoids that
# entire afternoon.

* text=auto

*.sh            text eol=lf
*.mjs           text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
.env.example    text eol=lf
*.example       text eol=lf

# Binary-ish: never touch.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
*.docx binary
*.tar.gz binary
